WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.000
This is a brief introduction to Positron on SageMaker Studio.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Now, at this point, I've already logged into my AWS account

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
and navigated into SageMaker Studio.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.000
And once I'm here, I can see that I have a Positron space

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.000
that's already running that I can open up,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.000
which we'll do in just a moment.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.000
If I don't already have an existing Positron space,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
these are actually created under the JupyterLab tab over here.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.000
So if I come over to the left-hand side,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.000
I click on JupyterLab, create a new JupyterLab space.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.000
We'll call this Positron example,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
and go ahead and create the space.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.000
When I create a space, the space doesn't automatically start.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Instead, it allows me to configure different details about the space.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Here I can change the instance size

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.000
to be something a little bit larger if I need to.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.000
And over here on the right-hand side is where I select the image

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.000
that this space runs off of.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Instead of the default SageMaker distribution image,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
I can click on this and then select a Positron image

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.000
that's been made available for me by my AWS account admin.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.000
If your account admin has not already configured

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
a Positron image to be available,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
details about how to do so are available in our administrator guide,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.000
step-by-step to walk through every part of the process

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.000
to make the Positron image available for users

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
to launch and create Positron spaces.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Now, I already have a space that's running,

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
so we're going to come back to our SageMaker Studio home,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
and then I can click Open, which will open Positron

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.000
in a new browser tab.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.000
As this opens, you'll notice that this is Positron

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.000
as you would expect it to be if you've been a previous user of this IDE.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.000
So I have Python and R installed and available.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
I can create different sessions for both Python and R execution,

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.000
and I have some additional features here

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:40.000
that make it really easy for me to work with other AWS resources and tools.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.000
So let's look at an example.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.000
If I open up a project here,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
now I have this project that has a number of different Python and R files

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.000
that I might want to interact with,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.000
and I have this application file that's already pulled up.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.000
If I click on Run here inside of Positron,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.000
this will launch this application.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:02.000
This shiny application runs here inside of my Positron environment.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Let's go ahead and let that run here.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.000
And what this does is this gives me sort of this chat-like interface.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Let's change the light mode here. There we go.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.000
This gives me this chat interface that allows me to interact with some data

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
that's hosted inside of Athena.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Because I'm already logged in and authenticated into AWS,

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.000
any sort of interaction I do with other AWS services,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.000
whether it's S3 or Athena or models on Bedrock,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.000
all of that can happen without me needing to reestablish credentials or identity.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.000
So in here I have this application that I've created in Positron,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:40.000
and then this application allows me to chat with this data

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.000
that's hosted inside of Athena.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.000
So if we choose, let's create a FIGAR risk plot here.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.000
The model that I'm interacting with is hosted on Bedrock,

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.000
and the data that I'm interacting with is hosted on Athena.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
So everything's happening natively inside of AWS.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.000
I don't have to establish any other permissions.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:59.000
And I get this sort of nice interface here that allows me to see,

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.000
okay, here's the command that I gave.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.000
We're going through and generating a few, looking at the data,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.000
making sure that we understand kind of the source of truth,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
and then creating this nice sort of charge-off rate by FICO band plot

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.000
with some interpretation that I can continue my conversation here.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.000
This sort of same pattern also exists inside of Posit Assistant.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.000
So if I come over to the left-hand sidebar, I can open up Posit Assistant.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.000
And this is the agent interface inside of Positron

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000
that allows me to interact with foundational AI models

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
for code development, data science, those types of tasks.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.000
So in here, if we create a new chat,

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.000
we can see some details about Posit Assistant.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.000
And if I come down here to the bottom,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.000
I can choose the model that I want to interact with,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.000
and I can see that I'm already configured automatically

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.000
to interact with available models through AWS Bedrock.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.000
So if I wanted to work with Sonnet 5 or GPT,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.000
different models that are available here inside of my Amazon environment,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.000
I can select this, and then I can come in and I can say,

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:05.000
let's create a simple Shiny app using the Diamonds data in R.

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Or whatever the case is. This is a fairly simple request,

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.000
but it's going to submit this request,

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.000
and then I can use Posit Assistant to evaluate and work with

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.000
either data that I have available to me inside of my environment,

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.000
data that's available inside of AWS,

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:22.000
or do things like build interactive applications

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.000
that I might want to share with broader users within my organization.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.000
As Posit Assistant is going through and starting to work on this task,

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.000
I can see down here that I'm keeping track of the tokens that I have,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.000
what's available inside of my context window,

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:39.000
as well as a cost estimate for how much this session has cost thus far.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.000
So there's some nice features here within Positron

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.000
that allow me to take advantage of the latest and greatest tools

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.000
in the AI space, but do so in a very sort of reproducible, governed way,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.000
alongside being able to sort of manage the cost

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
and usage of these tools as well.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:58.000
Now, like I mentioned, this is a very short introduction.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.000
If you'd like to learn more about how to take advantage of

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.000
and utilize Positron inside of SageMaker,

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.000
you can visit the user guide, which provides some additional guidance

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.000
and details about what's possible with this latest integration

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.000
with the Amazon ecosystem.

